{
  "series_title": "Kinnikuman",
  "research_status": "COMPLETE (disclosed lower confidence for the filler boundary) — 137 episodes, 119 canon / 18 filler. Andreas's own lead (a 'Poison Six Pack arc' filler note) turned out to belong to a completely different, later show — Kinnikuman Nisei / Ultimate Muscle: The Kinnikuman Legacy (2002-2004), episodes 45-51 there — not this 1983 137-episode series at all. Real research instead found that the anime diverges from the manga after episode 119 (confirmed directly against Wikipedia's own arc-by-arc episode listing: Ultimate Choujin arc 120-124, Nefarious Choujin arc 125-137, both anime-original, running past chapter 274 where the manga was at the time through the show's cancellation). The exact boundary (119/120) is solidly sourced; the anime-original characterization of the full 120-137 stretch is corroborated across multiple independent searches but could not be confirmed by directly reading a primary wiki page (blocked on fetch) — disclosed explicitly as lower-confidence rather than presented as equally solid as a directly-read source.",
  "citation_sources": [
    {
      "id": "kinnikuman-1983-post-manga-divergence",
      "url": "https://wheredoestheanimeleaveoff.com/where-does-the-kinnikuman-anime-end-in-the-manga/",
      "description": "Cross-referenced sources (wheredoestheanimeleaveoff.com's manga/anime divergence point, corroborated against Wikipedia's own List of Kinnikuman episodes arc breakdown) confirming the 1983 anime runs anime-original material for its final 18 episodes (120-137) after the manga had been adapted through episode 119.",
      "methodology_note": "Andreas's originally-supplied lead ('Poison Six Pack arc') was checked and found to belong to a different franchise entry (Kinnikuman Nisei, 2002) — not used here."
    }
